INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_development_metrics:false	- Enable registering development-oriented metrics on the internal `/metrics` endpoint, such as the per-method internal RPC latency histograms.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_developmental_unrecoverable_data_corrupting_features:	- Development features should never be enabled in a production cluster, or any cluster where stability, data loss, or the ability to upgrade are a concern. To enable experimental features, set the value of this configuration option to the current unix epoch expressed in seconds. The value must be within one hour of the current time on the broker. Once experimental features are enabled they cannot be disabled.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_host_metrics:true	- Enable exporting of some host metrics like /proc/diskstats, /proc/snmp and /proc/net/netstat
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_idempotence:true	- Enable idempotent producers.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_leader_balancer:true	- Enable automatic leadership rebalancing.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_listoffsets_historical_leader_epoch:false	- When enabled, the Kafka ListOffsets API returns the historical (record-time) leader epoch instead of the current leader epoch. Intended as a one-way opt-in: disabling after it has been enabled regresses to the original bug. Gated as a development feature: not all response paths are fixed yet (CORE-12505), so enabling this property produces internally inconsistent epoch values across paths and must not be enabled in production.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_metrics_reporter:true	- Enable the cluster metrics reporter. If `true`, the metrics reporter collects and exports to Redpanda Data a set of customer usage metrics at the interval set by `metrics_reporter_report_interval`. The cluster metrics of the metrics reporter are different from the monitoring metrics. * The metrics reporter exports customer usage metrics for consumption by Redpanda Data.* Monitoring metrics are exported for consumption by Redpanda users.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_mpx_extensions:false	- Enable Redpanda extensions for MPX.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_pid_file:true	- Enable PID file. You should not need to change.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_rack_awareness:false	- Enable rack-aware replica assignment.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_sasl:false	- Enable SASL authentication for Kafka connections. Authorization is required to modify this property. See also `kafka_enable_authorization`.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_schema_id_validation:none	- Mode to enable server-side schema ID validation. Accepted Values: * `none`: Schema validation is disabled (no schema ID checks are done). Associated topic properties cannot be modified. * `redpanda`: Schema validation is enabled. Only Redpanda topic properties are accepted. * `compat`: Schema validation is enabled. Both Redpanda and compatible topic properties are accepted.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_shadow_linking:false	- Enable creating Shadow Links from this cluster to a remote source cluster for data replication.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.enable_transactions:true	- Enable transactions (atomic writes).
