INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_catalog_commit_interval_ms:60000ms	- The frequency at which the Iceberg coordinator commits topic files to the catalog. This is the interval between commit transactions across all topics monitored by the coordinator, not the interval between individual commits.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_catalog_type:object_storage	- Iceberg catalog type that Redpanda will use to commit table metadata updates. Supported types: 'rest', 'object_storage'
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_default_catalog_namespace:["redpanda"]	- The default namespace (database name) for Iceberg tables. All tables created by Redpanda will be placed in this namespace within the Iceberg catalog. Supports nested namespaces as an array of strings. IMPORTANT: This value must be configured before enabling Iceberg and must not be changed afterward. Changing it will cause Redpanda to lose track of existing tables.
INFO  2026-10-01 00:06:49,879 [shard 0:main] main - application.cc:859 - redpanda.iceberg_default_partition_spec:(hour(redpanda.timestamp))	- Default value for the redpanda.iceberg.partition.spec topic property that determines the partition spec for the Iceberg table corresponding to the topic. If this property is not set and AWS Glue is being used as the Iceberg REST catalog, the default value will be overridden by an empty partition spec, for compatibility with AWS Glue.
